  "about": "The evangelium of the formulary “Saint Andrew the Apostle” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "At that time, as Jesus was walking beside the sea of Galilee, He saw two brothers, Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew his brother, throwing a net into the sea, for they were fishermen. And He said to them: “Come after Me, and I will make you become fishers of men.” And they, immediately leaving their nets, followed Him. And going on from there, He saw another pair of brothers, James the son of Zebedee and John his brother, in the boat with their father Zebedee, repairing their nets; and He called them. And they, at once leaving their nets and their father, followed Him.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w044", "w045"], "anchor": "w044", "gloss": "followed" }, { "words": ["w079", "w080"], "anchor": "w079", "gloss": "followed" }] }
  },
